From 1f7c83e0b7bc31897ebb9de30cc8b162b5428495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lotus contributors <build@givelotus.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:21:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Port shared Chronik host bridge to Bitcoin Core

Keep full witness bytes through private FFI, mempool and HTTP paths without changing public schemas or TxMut serialization. Adapt Core typed identifiers, validated-chain roles, native fee policy, optional admission-time coin snapshots and shared subscriber lifetime. Persist native block/undo and block-index metadata before index callbacks to recover after process crashes. Core has no Avalanche finality. This source overlay requires the matching exact-f13 native host mailbox; conservative per-block flush performance and cross-platform validation remain explicit follow-up work.

